% A string holding NUL bytes is written as a literal that spells them with
% the \0 escape, so that neither a terminal nor a line-oriented reader meets
% a NUL.  The csv and tsv formats copy a string's bytes as they are, which is
% why these strings are not among the values the other format tests share.
v(1, "\0").
v(2, "nul\0inside\0").
v(3, "\x00\x01").

v(N, V)?
